  "limitations": [
    "Only one Linux x86-64 development host was available; all browsers remain unsupported.",
    "The Firefox binary is a Playwright patched development build and cannot establish stable Firefox product support.",
    "The unpruned application AVM fails both decoded and compressed application payload budgets.",
    "Firefox timer-event p95 exceeds the active local-event target, and representative Chrome reruns expose startup and server-timing drift.",
    "The build samples cover dependency-cached profile packaging rather than a complete cold dependency and runtime-toolchain rebuild.",
    "Firefox JavaScript heap observation and parent-frame visibility into all runtime resources remain unavailable.",
    "Physical-device mobile, Safari, cross-platform, second-machine, thermal/power, and unavailable manual accessibility qualification is deferred to BH-22; mobile viability remains undecided.",
    "The measured fixtures and metric protocols remain BH-01 experimental evidence, not stable framework APIs or production readiness claims."
  ],
